<title>SINGAPORE: Dai Hung partners award Oct tender cargo to Exxon.</title>
<headline>Dai Hung partners award Oct tender cargo to Exxon.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The consortium operating the Dai Hung oil field, offshore Vietnam, have sold 450,000 barrels of the crude by tender to U.S. major Exxon, consortium sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said the October cargo was sold at Minas quotes plus 21 cents per barrel.</p>
<p>The consortium expects to issue another tender covering November barrels, a source said.  </p>
<p>Australia's Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd has a 43.75 percent state in the field. Other partners are Malaysia's Petronas Carigali with 20 percent, Vietnam's state-owned PetroVietnam with 15 percent, Total SA and Sumitomo Corp with 10.625 percent each.</p>
<p>In a previous tender, a September cargo was not awarded after failing to attract bids.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
</text>
